 "note": "Busselton-Sugito Japanese Friendship Garden, beside the Busselton Library (built 1998 by gardeners from Sugito, redesigned 2013), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and the City's sister-city book. The garden itself is under maples and paperbarks; what a driver sees is the mon (gateway) at the south entry from the library forecourt: two dark timber posts and a cross beam under a small gabled tiled roof, drawn with its doors shut. Inside, two large stone lanterns (toro) given by Sugito in 1999 and a small timber viewing platform; their exact spots are a guess. Front = south-south-east, to the forecourt. Metres: x west to east as seen from the forecourt, y north into the garden.",
